 we had been  able to spend time figuring that out  before we got there and uh we were very  prepared and we had to be because of the  situation we were in we just powered  through and i'm i'm so proud of  everybody who worked on this film uh  because they really managed to to step  up in a pretty challenging situation  i mean everything with the motorcycles  is pretty great i truly love claire  opening paddock nine and the first you  know jurassic world film running in high  heels with the flare and the glistening  sweat and just she was so sexy and  powerful and cool and it was like this  full circle moment  i love that she and she continues to  become even more badass in this movie  with like winning knife fights and you  know delivering one-liners and jumping  across alleyways from roof to roof and  you know it's it's real action hero  stuff it's just awesome that's what  stands out right now but there's so much  action it's hard to pick just one thing  yeah i've learned so much getting to  work with this guy because he is a true  action hero  and there were so many sequences that  started off basically being like a  60-second sequence and then a sequence  and then by the time chris was was done  performing it it was  an epic  uh kind of like three scene extravaganza  and he just he understands action  so innately and is constantly finding  moments for everyone else in the scene  to shine  and it's such a joy to work with him and  to and to watch him do his thing as well  two different answers uh the most  challenging was definitely the malta  sequence uh you know we  really changed the language of these  movies and the way that we shot it it  was it was handheld it was it was you  know moving at high speeds and and very  loose and uh and kind of junky and dirty  in ways that i that i was really excited  about doing uh but my favorite probably  is the scene with with claire and the  therazinosaurus because it feels like  the essence of what i love about  jurassi