 the credit  that he deserves and i think that that  need for recognition has driven him to  to keep pushing it and make a lot of you  know  really not so good decisions and in this  film he's gone a bit too far and he's  making this he's made a decision that  threatens the entire planet and i really  wanted him to have a moment of  redemption and a place where he really  has to decide you know which side of the  line is he gonna fall on and in this  film he makes a choice  that's another plane right  not exactly  well look the only thing that makes for  a perfect jurassic park movie is  jurassic park and i think once you  accept that and you know that that you  know as a filmmaker your goal is to to  take something that is a perfectly  tended garden and then plant something  new respecting uh the foundation that  that movie was built on and it was built  on science and it was built on a  question asked by michael crichton uh  about our our place in this world and  our responsibility uh  in the shadow of of nature and and its  power and hopefully we've asked that  question in this film in a way that that  honors uh what he did  well you know it is the end of an of  this story that we've been telling and  at the end of these six movies uh and  yet in this film it was really important  to us to introduce new characters and  new heroes that fans and and especially  the next generation can  can uh want to follow and i'm i'm  confident they will so for me  i know that there's a young filmmaker  out there who has the passion for this  uh that i have and that i had eight or  nine years ago that'll see this new  world that we've created and know what  story uh there is to tell so whoever you  are if he or she is out there we're  listening i think i i think i've told my  story i think i've told my story i think  it's it's good to pass the torch i had  the torch pass to me and i think it's my  responsibility to pass it to somebody  else  you
 

